# Peer resolution is relaxed for one reason, and it is no longer Polaris.
#
# WAS: Polaris 13 declared React 18 peers while the app runs React 19, and
# npm's ERESOLVE killed fresh installs. Polaris is gone (the embedded Shopify
# app moved to peakhour-shopify and uses Polaris WEB COMPONENTS from Shopify's
# CDN), so that reason has expired.
#
# IS: this repo runs typescript ^6, and typescript-eslint 8.57.2 — with eight
# sibling @typescript-eslint/* packages, pulled in transitively by
# eslint-config-next — still declares `typescript >=4.8.4 <6.0.0`. That edge is
# genuinely unsatisfiable, not cosmetic: `npm install --strict-peer-deps` exits
# 1 on it. It survives today only because npm 10 and 11 downgrade it to
# `npm warn ERESOLVE overriding peer dependency` in their default non-strict
# mode.
#
# Vercel sets no installCommand, and this repo pins no `engines` field and has
# no .nvmrc, so the npm version that builds production is not ours to choose.
# Relying on a warning staying a warning across an npm version we do not
# control is a bet with a production build on the other side of it.
#
# REMOVE THIS FILE when typescript-eslint's peer range admits TS 6 — at that
# point run `npm install --strict-peer-deps` and confirm it exits 0.
legacy-peer-deps=true
